<title>CHINA: HK Association of Banks leaves rates unchanged.</title>
<headline>HK Association of Banks leaves rates unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Association of Banks announced on Friday that it would keep deposit interest rates unchanged.</p>
<p>The group also said prime rates would not be changed.</p>
<p>Prime rates were last increased in March 1997, when banks raised rates by 25 basis points to 8.75 percent.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636</p>
